WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.568
-Thank you very much, everybody.
Thank you.

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:05.538
Thank you, thank you.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:08.007
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.943
Everyone's indoors watching
the show tonight, cozy.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:12.178
I love it.
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.846
We're having
a sleepover tonight.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.248
We're having a sleepover.
It's gonna be fun.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.417
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.251
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:21.521
Well, guys, as if things
aren't crazy enough,

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.756
right now, millions of people
on the East Coast

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:26.192
are bracing for some
pretty intense weather.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.994
-A blockbuster nor'easter.

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:30.263
-A beast of a December
snowstorm.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.732
-Nightmarish, major, and epic.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:35.501
-Tens of millions bracing
for a powerful winter storm

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.970
that could bring up
to two feet of snow.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.573
-Yep. When the experts said
stay home and hunker down,

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.543
Americans were like,
"We're already home

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.844
and we're already hunkered."

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.580
Yeah, yeah.
Instead of a snow day tomorrow,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.450
a lot of kids
will have school remotely.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.884
That's where your 6-year-old
just said,

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:54.787
"2020 can go straight
to H-E-double hockey sticks."

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.889
Hey.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:58.657
I got to be honest.
I'm not really looking forward

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:01.060
to starting my day tomorrow
by using an ice scraper

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.696
on my face shield.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.965
Well, here in New York City,
Mayor Bill de Blasio

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:09.102
said that while street
dining must close for the storm,

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.771
sidewalk dining can remain open.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.740
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.009
That sounds like fun
during a blizzard,

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.811
especially when your waiter
has to curl your entree

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.246
over to you with a broom.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:24.184 line:0%
"Who ordered the steak? Here we
go. Okay, go, go, go, go."

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:28.487
Yeah, sidewalk dining
will remain open

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:30.423
because what's more fun
than eating a plate

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.325
of frozen pasta while a plow

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.927
blasts you with
a foot of gray sludge?

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.596
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.030
Yep, thanks to the blizzard,

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.633
millions of people
could end up losing power

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.568
or, as one man put it,
[as Trump] join the club.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.538
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:49.608 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:52.545
A lot of Republicans say
the power's still on, actually.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.447
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.982
[ Normal voice ]
Sir, no one can hear you.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.983
The televisions are off.
There's no electricity.

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.719
[ as Trump ] Yes, it is.
There's electricity.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.453
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:02.788
[ Normal voice ] By the way,
you know we're entering

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:05.424
the post-Trump world
when our monologues start with

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.760
"Hey, guys, some big news about
the weather."

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.129
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:12.698
Feels kind of good!

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:14.066
Well, everyone's talking
about this.

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:17.269
Tom Cruise was caught on tape
yelling at his crew,

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:18.537
but he was basically
just telling them

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.906
to socially distance
and be safe from COVID.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:22.375
Here, listen to this.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:38.591
Yeah, wow, if Tom Cruise
worked in the White House,

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.559
we could have had
the vaccine back in April.

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:44.330
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.998
For the last nine months,
that's pretty much

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:48.101
how Dr. Fauci has
felt on the inside.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.936
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.004
What's amazing is when
Tom delivered that rant,

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.540
he was hanging off
a 163-story building.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.509
Isn't that amazing?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.509 --> 00:02:59.144
But actually, this isn't
the first time a celebrity

00:02:59.144 --> 00:03:00.580
has been caught ranting
about something

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.048
that has turned out
to be pretty helpful advice.

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:04.684
Check out some of these
other examples.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:58.104
Helpful, helpful,
helpful advice.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.273
We're submitting that
for the Emmys show.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.842
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.344
Well, guys, it's been
a tough week for President Trump

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:07.546
and it keeps getting worse.
Now, his next-door neighbors

00:04:07.546 --> 00:04:09.482 line:0%
at Mar-a-Lago are saying
they don't want him

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:12.485 line:0%
to live there
after he leaves the White House.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.453
Neighbors are like,
"This is a classy area.

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:17.023
We can't be associated
with a one-term president."

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.624
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:20.927
New York doesn't want him.
Mar-a-Lago doesn't want him.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.895
Man, one minute you're waking up
in the White House,

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.396
next, you're waking up
next to Lou Dobbs,

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:25.998
whispering, "I made us coffee."

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:28.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.637
I'm not surprised nobody wants
Trump living next door.

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.172
Most neighbors ask
to borrow some sugar.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:36.876
Trump's like,
"Can I borrow $400 million?"

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.878
It would be ironic, though,
if Trump does move there

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:41.013
and then his neighbors
build a giant wall next to him.

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.849
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.183
Just saying.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.719
We'll pay for it.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:50.289
Changing gears here, I saw that
IKEA is now selling tiny homes

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:53.159
starting around $47,000.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.127
Yeah, it sounds interesting,
but I'm not sure if I want

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:57.363
to live in a house I assembled
with an Allen wrench.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:58.931
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.299
You know that uneasy feeling

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:01.334
when you're done
building a dresser

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.836
and there's like
three extra pieces?

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.138
Now picture that with a house.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.639
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.241 line:0%
Listen to this.
In a new study,

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.742 line:0%
45% of people
working remotely admitted

00:05:10.742 --> 00:05:12.879 line:0%
they drink during the work day,

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:14.714
as opposed to the other 55%

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.349
who still do it
but didn't admit it.

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:17.783
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.285
Meanwhile, there's also
another survey

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.153
that found that college kids
are actually drinking

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:23.656
less during the pandemic.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:26.258
Turns out it's not that fun
to do a keg stand

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:28.161
when the people holding your
legs are your mom and dad.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.729
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.330
And finally,
a documentary filmmaker

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.566
made a little mistake
while he was flying over Brazil.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:34.734
Watch this.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.902 line:0%
-A documentary filmmaker
got a little careless

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:39.705 line:0%
while snapping pictures
from a small plane over Brazil.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:42.909 line:0%
His iPhone 6S slipped out
of his hand

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:45.545 line:0%
and plunged 1,000 feet
to the ground,

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:48.680 line:0%
and it recorded the entire
15-second fall.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.951 line:0%
-Thanks to GPS, he found
that phone the next day,

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:56.289 line:0%
still charged with only a crack
in the protective screen.

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:58.057
-Get out of here!
-What?

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.692
-That's crazy.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:02.061
I mean, who the hell still
has an iPhone 6?

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:04.530
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.565
That's right.
His iPhone only had one crack

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:08.334
after falling 1,000 feet.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.102
Meanwhile, I dropped mine
in the parking lot.

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:11.971
Looks like a monster truck
drove over it.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.506
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:17.743
Joining us in studio, she stars
in the new animated Pixar film,

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:20.545
"Soul" -- Tina Fey is here!

00:06:20.545 --> 00:06:24.316
[ Cheers and applause ]
Tina Fey!

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:26.385
Plus, she directed, produced
and co-wrote

00:06:26.385 --> 00:06:29.021
the upcoming film
"Wonder Woman 1984."

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.823
Patty Jenkins is here!

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:32.859
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:35.194
And we got great music,
my friend upstate,

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:38.764
my friend "Q-Ball,"
Shawn Quinlan upstate,

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:40.532
was telling me
all the music he was into.

00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:43.068
He's like, "Have you heard
this kid, Marcus King?"

00:06:43.068 --> 00:06:44.703
Do you know Marcus King?

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.806
-I'm still tripping
off of Q-Ball.

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:48.173
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.173 --> 00:06:50.642
Is that his real name?
-That's his real name.

00:06:50.642 --> 00:06:52.478
-Does he know
you call him Q-Ball?

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:53.880
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, I call him

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.981
a bunch of, like, fun,
friend nicknames.

00:06:55.981 --> 00:06:57.984
-What's he call you?

00:06:57.984 --> 00:07:01.120
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.256
-Jim.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.256 --> 00:07:05.490
It's not Jimmy.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.559
-"Hey, Jimothy, what's up, man?
It's Q-Ball."

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:10.295
-No, Jimothy is --
Some people call me Jimothy.

00:07:10.295 --> 00:07:12.631
But no, he -- we're
straight up -- Jim he calls me.

00:07:12.631 --> 00:07:14.800
Yeah, which is kind of
a fun nickname.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.502
-Straight up Jim.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:19.405
-You know, Quinlan
is his last name.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:20.606
-Oh, okay.
-So he's Q-Ball.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:21.706
-Yeah, Q-Ball.

00:07:21.706 --> 00:07:24.810
-Shawn. Shawn Quinlan.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.078
Quinlan, Q-Ball.

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:28.915
I call him Shawn. I call him Q.

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:31.150
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.619
-He doesn't know
you call him Q-Ball.

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.821
-Yeah.
-He answers the phone.

00:07:35.821 --> 00:07:37.589
He's like, "Hello?" You're like,
"Hey, Q-Ball, what's up?

00:07:37.589 --> 00:07:39.992
It's J-Jim."
He's like, "What?"

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:43.296
-I don't say it's J-J-Jim.
I say it's Jim.

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:44.830
I know who it is if I'm calling.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.231
-Okay. Cool.
-Yeah.

00:07:46.231 --> 00:07:48.000
You kind of hesitated a little
bit when you said my name.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.368
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:52.371
No, I know my name.
-Alright, alright, Jim-Ball.

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:54.440
-Jim-Ball is not a thing
that no one --

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.108
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:57.977
-It'll catch on.
-It won't catch on.

00:07:57.977 --> 00:07:59.778
I don't want it to catch on.

00:07:59.778 --> 00:08:02.815
I want Jimmy. James is my name.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:04.616
I used to go by Jim
all the time.

00:08:04.616 --> 00:08:06.652
Then I like Jimmy Fallon,

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:09.088
then my rap name
was Colgate for a while.

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:12.691
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.691 --> 00:08:15.962
-I think I can guess why.

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.497
-The toothpaste.

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.564
-I mean, extra fresh,
I don't know.

00:08:19.564 --> 00:08:20.866
-Oh, man, I wish
I thought of that.

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:22.034
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:23.469
-Oh, damn!
-Wow!

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:26.939
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.240
-Wait, are you
going back in time?

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:30.810
-Yeah. I never thought that.
That's actually good.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.545
My rhymes weren't that good.
-Extra fresh.

00:08:32.545 --> 00:08:33.712
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.712 --> 00:08:35.982
-Anyway, I'm talking to Q-Ball.

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:37.082
I go, "What's up?
What are you listening to?"

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:39.184
He goes,
"Check out Marcus King."

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:41.086
This dude shreds.
He's got a great voice.

00:08:41.086 --> 00:08:43.222
I love it. Get ready.
You're going to love this guy.

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:44.723
Marcus King
is on the show tonight.

00:08:44.723 --> 00:08:49.094
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:49.094 --> 00:08:52.331
So, I watched "Soul" over
the weekend, the Pixar movie,

00:08:52.331 --> 00:08:55.735
Tina Fey, Jamie Foxx --
they're both fantastic in it.

00:08:55.735 --> 00:08:58.504
The movie's great, man. Oh, man.

00:08:58.504 --> 00:09:01.607
Guess whose first voice
or second voice you hear

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:03.309
in the whole thing.
-My boy Q-Ball.

00:09:03.309 --> 00:09:04.610
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.879
-Q-Ball! Questlove! Yeah!
Q-Ball! That's right, Questlove!

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:09.648
-Q-Ball! Q-Ball!

00:09:09.648 --> 00:09:11.249
-[ Laughing ]
You call him Q-Ball?

00:09:11.249 --> 00:09:14.052
-Yeah, man.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.052 --> 00:09:16.722
-Questlove is in "Soul."

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:19.257
Here he is as Curly.
Look at this.

00:09:19.257 --> 00:09:21.660
-And I'm bald-headed.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.195
-You're like a cue ball.
-Yeah.

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:25.498
-Yeah, you're bald
as a cue ball.

00:09:25.498 --> 00:09:28.300
Curly -- Quest,
you are fantastic in this.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.835
-Thank you.
-I heard your voice.

00:09:29.835 --> 00:09:32.137
I knew we talked about
this months ago,

00:09:32.137 --> 00:09:34.573
and you said you're in this,
but you're really good in this.

00:09:34.573 --> 00:09:36.809
-Thank you.
When they called me to --

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:38.244
When they pitched it to me,

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:41.346
I thought they just wanted
recommendations for music

00:09:41.346 --> 00:09:42.714
because it was like
an 11-minute pitch.

00:09:42.714 --> 00:09:44.616
I'm like, "Who gives
an 11-minute pitch for music?"

00:09:44.616 --> 00:09:45.918
-Yeah, I'll figure it out.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:47.185
-I was like, well, yeah,
I can recommend some people.

00:09:47.185 --> 00:09:49.521
And they're like,
"No, you're in it."

00:09:49.521 --> 00:09:52.491
-Wow!
-I just fell out, like...

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:54.993
-It's wild. I mean,
the movie is a trip, man.

00:09:54.993 --> 00:09:57.563
It's really amazing.

00:09:57.563 --> 00:09:58.831
You forget you're watching --
I mean,

00:09:58.831 --> 00:10:00.866
the animation is just amazing.

00:10:00.866 --> 00:10:03.002
But it's great. It's moving.

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:06.739
But, dude, you're perfect.
-It's really for adults, though.

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:08.140
It's for adults.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:11.343
-I watched it with my girls.
They dug it. They liked it.

00:10:11.343 --> 00:10:13.112
-But you felt that
a little bit more, didn't you?

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:14.847
-Phew, man, I was weeping.
I felt it.

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:17.816
-Exactly. [ Laughs ]
-"Don't even look at me."

00:10:17.816 --> 00:10:20.252
I had my kids sitting on my lap
so they couldn't see me.

00:10:20.252 --> 00:10:22.621
-Right.
-Gosh, dude.

00:10:22.621 --> 00:10:24.323
Wait till you see what you do
with your life, you know?

00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:25.591
It's like, oh, my God.
-Exactly.

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:27.092
-It's one of those movies.
-Yeah.

00:10:27.092 --> 00:10:29.428
-But, dude, you're great in it.

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:31.497
What do you think the jazz club
that they're imitating,

00:10:31.497 --> 00:10:32.832
which one do you --
I think it's --

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:35.000
Downstairs looks like
Jazz Standard.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:39.004
-I felt that it -- What's the
one that goes on Sixth Avenue

00:10:39.004 --> 00:10:41.940
that goes downstairs?

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:43.141
Village Vanguard.

00:10:43.141 --> 00:10:45.077
-The outside looks like
Vanguard to me.

00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:46.745
-Yeah.
-But it's called the Half Notes.

00:10:46.745 --> 00:10:49.148
So I thought, oh.
-Oh, Blue Note.

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:51.783
Yeah, Blue Note.
-But then I think --

00:10:51.783 --> 00:10:52.918
Yeah, I guess Village Vanguard.

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:54.420
-I felt like
it was Village Vanguard.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.622
-It's Vanguard, yeah, yeah.

00:10:56.622 --> 00:10:58.591
I mean, the details in those
movies are just fantastic.

00:10:58.591 --> 00:11:01.394
But we'll talk to Tina later
about being in this.

00:11:01.394 --> 00:11:06.832
But Q-Ball, Questlove, Ahmir,
Questlove Thompson is in "Soul."

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:08.334
And you crush it, buddy.
-Thank you.

00:11:08.334 --> 00:11:10.168
-Congrats on that. That's got
to feel good to be in that.

00:11:10.168 --> 00:11:12.804
Everyone, we have exactly
three shows left

00:11:12.804 --> 00:11:14.840
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.642
that beloved "Tonight Show"
tradition.

00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:20.712
It is time for "12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters!"

00:11:20.712 --> 00:11:22.881
♪ -12 days of
Christmas sweaters ♪

00:11:22.881 --> 00:11:26.886
♪ Three days left ♪

00:11:26.886 --> 00:11:29.454
-That's right. Every show
between now and Christmas,

00:11:29.454 --> 00:11:32.925
we'll be giving one lucky
audience member a breathtaking

00:11:32.925 --> 00:11:37.195
Christmas sweater from the
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:11:37.195 --> 00:11:39.531
Now, since there are
three shows left,

00:11:39.531 --> 00:11:42.434
let's open door number three.

00:11:42.434 --> 00:11:44.303
[ Drumroll ]

00:11:44.303 --> 00:11:47.973
Where is it? Oh, yeah,
I see it up there, yeah.

00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:49.274
Ooh, wow!

00:11:49.274 --> 00:11:51.009
This is...moving.

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:54.280 line:0%
♪♪

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:55.914
Wow, that --

00:11:55.914 --> 00:11:58.216
It looks like it's still alive,
that sweater.

00:11:58.216 --> 00:12:01.153
Oh, my gosh.
Can we dim the lights there?

00:12:01.153 --> 00:12:02.821
[ Audience oohs ]

00:12:02.821 --> 00:12:06.458
Yes, flip it around.
Let's see the back.

00:12:06.458 --> 00:12:08.393
Oh, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:12:08.393 --> 00:12:09.762
Yeah. Alright.

00:12:09.762 --> 00:12:11.530
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:12.965
Everyone,
look at your seat number.

00:12:12.965 --> 00:12:14.500
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.235
Quest, can I get a drumroll,
please?

00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:19.672
[ Drumroll ]

00:12:19.672 --> 00:12:22.040
1-4-2!

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:27.446 line:0%
♪♪

00:12:27.446 --> 00:12:32.885 line:0%
♪♪

00:12:32.885 --> 00:12:35.954
Congratulations. You won
tonight's Christmas sweater.

00:12:35.954 --> 00:12:37.989
What is your name?
-Katherine.

00:12:37.989 --> 00:12:39.024
-Katherine, where are you from?

00:12:39.024 --> 00:12:40.893
-New York.
-New York. Oh, my gosh.

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:42.962
Can you try that guy on
so we see what it looks like?

00:12:42.962 --> 00:12:44.763
-Yeah.

00:12:44.763 --> 00:12:46.898
-There's no real...

00:12:46.898 --> 00:12:49.368
There's no real front or back
to these this year.

00:12:49.368 --> 00:12:50.703
We kind of went...

00:12:50.703 --> 00:12:53.004
Yeah, that's the back, actually.

00:12:53.004 --> 00:12:55.441
But it doesn't matter.
It doesn't matter.

00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:58.343
There should be a hole
for your head somewhere.

00:12:58.343 --> 00:13:00.646
Look at this. Even backwards,
it's going to look good.

00:13:00.646 --> 00:13:05.417 line:0%
♪♪

00:13:05.417 --> 00:13:06.451
[ Laughs ]

00:13:06.451 --> 00:13:07.986
Ooh!

00:13:07.986 --> 00:13:11.523
Wow! Look at that! Gorgeous!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:11.523 --> 00:13:13.225
That is what I'm talking about!

00:13:13.225 --> 00:13:17.262
Stunning! Congratulations!
Oh, my gosh.

00:13:17.262 --> 00:13:19.231
Another round of applause
for our winner right there.

00:13:19.231 --> 00:13:20.699
Thanks again to
our lucky audience member.

00:13:20.699 --> 00:13:23.935
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Tina Fey, everybody!

00:13:23.935 --> 00:13:25.237
Come on back!

